From 00c33d94dbcea53e4eaf1cb9428c7b13a1ce421f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Maiorano <amaiorano@google.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:29:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-113252: Improper input validation in
 ANGLE

Manual backport of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8502520:
D3D11: Fix UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH handling in fast PBO unpack

In PixelTransfer11::setBufferToTextureCopyParams, PixelsPerRow was set
to unpack.rowLength (when > 0) instead of destArea.width. Because
PixelsPerRow controls the number of destination columns drawn per row,
setting it to unpack.rowLength caused incomplete row writes when 0 <
unpack.rowLength < destArea.width and out-of-bounds row writes when
unpack.rowLength > destArea.width on partial-width updates.

Set PixelsPerRow to destArea.width and compute RowStride from
unpack.rowLength (when > 0) or destArea.width.

Also move PBO unpack validation and hardened-context unpack parameter
validation from ValidateES3TexImageParametersBase into
ValidImageDataSize so ES2 contexts with GL_EXT_unpack_subimage and
GL_NV_pixel_buffer_object enforce the same checks as ES3.

Add tests:
- Texture2DTestES3.TexImageUnpackRowLengthSmallerThanWidthAndSubRectPBO
- WebGL1CompatibilityTest.UnpackStateAndPBOValidation

Skip
Texture2DTestES3.TexImageUnpackRowLengthSmallerThanWidthAndSubRectPBO on
PIXEL10 GLES (PowerVR), where the native GLES driver fails with
GL_INVALID_OPERATION when unpacking overlapping rows (0 <
GL_UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH < width) from a PBO, matching existing skips under
crbug.com/480069042.

Bug: b/556750258
